version downgrades, once the metadata version is upgraded to support this feature, it cannot be downgraded to a version that doesn't support it.\\\\n\\\\n**Source:** `/store/kips/KIP-1266/2026-01-20-mail-b3176fec.md` (lines 24-40)\\\",\\\"error\\\":null,\\\"files\\\":[\\\"store\\\",\\\"kips/KIP-1266/2026-01-12-mail-discuss-remote-log-metadata-3c39548c.md\\\",\\\"kips/KIP-1266/2026-01-14-mail-d0eb8ce129ffef70296f85a7-de7d95c0.md\\\",\\\"kips/KIP-1266/2026-01-15-mail-d42ec61c1696ad3122663d8a-ab534859.md\\\",\\\"kips/KIP-1266/2026-01-18-mail-422fb6a7.md\\\",\\\"kips/KIP-1266/2026-01-20-mail-b3176fec.md\\\",\\\"kips/KIP-1266/mail-25888a786e32c109db6ea259-737a72b0.md\\\"],\\\"seconds\\\":20.68,\\\"truncated\\\":false,\\\"turns\\\":2,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"cache_read_tokens\\\":117747,\\\"cache_write_tokens\\\":41758,\\\"cost_usd\\\":0.1046687,\\\"input_tokens\\\":58,\\\"output_tokens\\\":1864}}\"}","_meta":{"fastmcp":{"wrap_result":true}},"structuredContent":{"result":"{\"answer\":\"Based on my search of the context filesystem, I found the answer to your question in the KIP-1266 discussion.\\n\\n## Answer\\n\\nThe mechanism proposed to gate the introduction of new tombstone semantics and additional record fields during rolling upgrades for the remote log segment metadata topic in tiered storage is **metadata version gating**.\\n\\nAccording to the KIP-1266 discussion, Lijun Tong explains:\\n\\n> \\\"The solution I have in mind is this feature is *gated by the metadata version*. The new tombstone semantics and the additional fields (for example in RemoteLogSegmentUpdateRecord) are only enabled once the cluster metadata version is upgraded to the version that introduces this feature. As long as the cluster metadata version is not bumped, the system will not produce tombstone records. Therefore, during rolling upgrades (mixed 4.2/4.3 brokers), the feature remains effectively disabled. Tombstones will only start being produced after the metadata version is upgraded, at which point all brokers are already required to support the new behavior.\\\"\\n\\nThis approach ensures that during rolling upgrades with mixed broker versions, the feature remains disabled until all brokers are upgraded and the metadata version is explicitly bumped. Additionally, since Kafka does not support metadata version downgrades, once the metadata version is upgraded to support this feature, it cannot be downgraded to a version that doesn't support it.\\n\\n**Source:** `/store/kips/KIP-1266/2026-01-20-mail-b3176fec.md` (lines 24-40)\",\"error\":null,\"files\":[\"store\",\"kips/KIP-1266/2026-01-12-mail-discuss-remote-log-metadata-3c39548c.md\",\"kips/KIP-1266/2026-01-14-mail-d0eb8ce129ffef70296f85a7-de7d95c0.md\",\"kips/KIP-1266/2026-01-15-mail-d42ec61c1696ad3122663d8a-ab534859.md\",\"kips/KIP-1266/2026-01-18-mail-422fb6a7.md\",\"kips/KIP-1266/2026-01-20-mail-b3176fec.md\",\"kips/KIP-1266/mail-25888a786e32c109db6ea259-737a72b0.md\"],\"seconds\":20.68,\"truncated\":false,\"turns\":2,\"usage\":{\"cache_read_tokens\":117747,\"cache_write_tokens\":41758,\"cost_usd\":0.1046687,\"input_tokens\":58,\"output_tokens\":1864}}"}}}
